<title>UK: Body Shop up as Merrill rates &quot;accumulate&quot;.</title>
<headline>Body Shop up as Merrill rates &quot;accumulate&quot;.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Body Shop International Plc rose on Monday after the stock was raised to an intermediate-term &quot;accumulate&quot; from &quot;neutral&quot; at Merrill Lynch, market sources said.</p>
<p>The stock was up 4p at 205-1/2 by 1239 GMT in thin volume of 51,623 shares.</p>
<p>Sources said the upgrade reflected hopes for improved trading news from the United States for the cosmetics and toiletries retailer. Analysts at the brokerage were not immediately available for comment.</p>
<p>-- David Holmes, London Newsroom +44 171 542 5106</p>
